row.entry:
pMD20 containing 1289 base pairs of cloned DNA sequence containing PBAT hydrolase (PBATH
                              Bp
                           ) gene from NKCM3201

ce:section.ce:para:
Poly(butylene adipate-co-terephthalate) (PBAT; Fig. 1
                        ), poly(ethylene succinate) (PESu), polycaprolactone (PCL), poly(butylene succinate) (PBSu), poly(butylene succinate-co-adipate) (PBSA), poly(3-hydroxybutyrate) (P(3HB)), and poly(lactic acid) (PLA) were kindly supplied by BASF Japan Ltd., NIPPON SHOKUBAI CO., LTD., Daicel Corporation., Showa Denko K.K., MITSUBISHI GAS CHEMICAL COMPANY, INC., and Mitsui Chemicals Inc., respectively. Before use, they were dissolved in chloroform and were precipitated in methanol to purify. After these precipitates were collected, they were dried in vacuo. Polyester films (1 × 1 × 0.1 cm3) of polyesters were prepared by cooling them to 20 °C after melt-pressed with a mini Test Press-10 (Toyo seiki Seisaku-Sho, Ltd.). After washing of the films with methanol and distilled water, the films were dried in vacuo. TaKaRa Ex Taq
                        ®, T-Vector pMD20, T4 DNA ligase, expression vector pNCMO2, restriction enzymes, and PrimeSTAR® HS DNA Polymerase were purchased from Takara Bio Inc. Oligonucleotides were purchased from Eurofins Genomics K.K. Other chemicals were purchased from WAKO Pure Chemical Industries, Ltd. and Sigma-Aldrich Co., LLC.

16S rDNA sequences of 3 isolates (strain NKCM3101, NKCM3201, and NKCM3202) were deposited in the DNA Databank of Japan (DDBJ) under the accession numbers LC034565, LC034563, and LC034564 (Fig. 2
                        ). pbath

                           Bp
                         and its 3 mutant genes (S77A, D133 N, and H156 N) were also deposited in DDBJ under the accession numbers LC189557, LC189558, LC189559, and LC189560 (Fig. 3
                        ).
